{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe Paris heat is a beast, but the evening air on Montmartre was glorious. We visited the abattoirs today; a grim spectacle of industry, yet one must see the machinery of the city. We also inspected the Bourse and the Chamber of Deputies. The latter is grand, but I confess the former held more interest.\n\nDined at 5:30 with Cousin and Fauriel. Cousin is as brilliant and insufferable as ever; he speaks of history as if he invented it. Fauriel, the Greek song editor, is charming and ate with great enthusiasm. The food was excellent, the wine even better, and the bill, though stiff, was worth it for the conversation. Mignet and Thiers were absent, but their absence was felt.\n\nI hope the boys are well and that Karl’s studies in logic are progressing without too much fuss. I miss your quiet, but the road is long.\n\nYours,\nG.W.F."}}],"created":1795219390,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":211,"prompt_tokens":1132,"total_tokens":1343,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-6ODakcdDyO5aBTdyDQKrCkiS4dmyKKqR","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":1132,"prompt_ms":1179.117,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.0416227915194345,"prompt_per_second":960.0404370389028,"predicted_n":211,"predicted_ms":4976.219,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.696280952380953,"predicted_per_second":42.20071504087742}}